      'Kapha properties: Guru (heavy), Sheeta (cold), Mrudu (soft), Snigdha (unctuous), Madhura (sweet), Sthira (stable), Pichchhila (slimy) - seven qualities',
      'Diseases treated with drugs having Viparita Guna (opposite properties) - the cornerstone of pharmacological treatment',
      'Four objectives of life: Dharma (virtue), Artha (wealth), Kama (gratification), Moksha (emancipation) - Health (Arogya) is the root of all four',
      'Trisutra: Hetu-Linga-Aushadha knowledge applies to both Swastha (healthy) for prevention and Atura (sick) for cure',
