    additionalTopics: [
      { title: 'Trivrit as Best Purgative', content: 'Trivrit (Operculina turpethum) is the best general purgative. Properties: Madhura Vipaka, Ushna Virya, Laghu-Snigdha Guna. Action: clears Pitta and Kapha from Pakvashaya. Dose: 3-5g powder with warm water or honey. Onset: 3-6 hours. Expected: 4-8 purges.', clinicalRelevance: 'Trivrit is the first-choice purgative for most Virechana procedures.' },
      { title: 'Virechana Drug Selection by Prakriti', content: 'Vata Prakriti: Trivrit + Eranda + warm milk. Pitta Prakriti: Trivrit + Draksha + sugar. Kapha Prakriti: Danti + Trivrit + honey. Obese patients: higher dose. Lean patients: lower dose. Strong Agni: Tikshna drugs. Weak Agni: mild drugs.', clinicalRelevance: 'Individualized Virechana drug selection improves efficacy.' },
      { title: 'Basti Drug Classification', content: 'Niruha (decoction enema): Kashaya + honey + salt + oil. Anuvasana (oil enema): plain or medicated oil. Matra Basti (small oil enema): 60ml daily. Uttar Basti (uro-genital enema): specialized for urinary and reproductive disorders.', clinicalRelevance: 'Basti classification enables precise selection based on disease.' },
    ],
