    doshaDiscussion: [
      'Excessive visual stimulation (TV, screens, bright light): Pitta vitiation in eyes - causes burning, redness, headache',
      'Deficient visual stimulation (darkness, lack of visual variety): Vata-Kapha - causes dry eyes, heaviness, poor vision',
      'Excessive noise (loud music, constant noise): Pitta-Rakta vitiation - causes tinnitus, headache, irritability',
      'Deficient auditory stimulation (silence deprivation): Vata - causes anxiety, restlessness, sleep disturbance',
      'Excessive olfactory stimulation (strong perfumes, chemicals): Pitta vitiation - causes headache, nausea, nasal congestion',
      'Excessive taste stimulation (very spicy, very sour): Pitta-Kapha vitiation - causes mouth ulcers, digestive disorders',
      'Excessive touch stimulation (rough clothing, extreme temperatures): Vata-Pitta vitiation - causes skin disorders, pain',
      'Mental dosha (Rajas, Tamas) directly affect sensory function - Rajas causes overstimulation, Tamas causes understimulation',
    ],
    treatmentPrinciples: [
      'Sattvavajaya Chikitsa (psychological therapy): Jnana (knowledge of self), Vijnana (scientific understanding), Dhairya (patience), Smriti (memory), Samadhi (meditation)',
      'Indriya Sevana Vidhi: proper use of each sense organ as preventive medicine',
      'Proper visual hygiene: avoid excessive screen time, bright lights, and darkness. Use Triphala wash for eyes.',
      'Proper auditory hygiene: avoid excessive noise, practice silence, use ear oils for nourishment',
      'Proper olfactory hygiene: avoid strong chemicals, use pleasant aromas, Nasya for nasal health',
      'Proper gustatory hygiene: balanced diet with all six tastes, avoid extreme tastes in excess',
      'Proper tactile hygiene: comfortable clothing, moderate temperatures, regular Abhyanga',
      'Lifestyle modification for sensory balance: Dinacharya, Ritucharya, Sadvritta',
    ],
