    additionalTopics: [
      { title: 'Chatushpada in Modern Healthcare', content: 'Physician: qualified, experienced, skilled, ethical. Medicine: evidence-based, quality-assured, available. Attendant: trained nursing staff with technical skill and compassion. Patient: compliant, informed, truthful, courageous. All four must be present for successful treatment.', clinicalRelevance: 'Chatushpada model is directly applicable to modern healthcare.' },
      { title: 'Patient Selection and Prognosis', content: 'Treatable patient: good memory, courage, obedience, truthfulness. Untreatable: poor memory, fear, disobedience, dishonesty. Also consider: disease treatability, patient strength, compliance potential, support system.', clinicalRelevance: 'Patient selection is as important as disease diagnosis.' },
    ],
    importantVerses: [
      'Four components of treatment: physician, medicine, attendant, and patient - each with four qualities (9.3)',
      'Physician: theoretically learned, practically experienced, dexterous, and pure (9.4)',
      'All four components must be present for successful treatment. Deficiency in any reduces success (9.8)',
      'The physician is the most important among the four components - the primary cause of treatment success (9.10)',
      'Patient: good memory, courageous, obedient, and truthful (9.7)',
    ],
