      'Select appropriate treatment (Upakrama): Shamana for mild, Shodhana for severe, Rasayana for chronic, combined for complex',
      'Execute with physician skill (Vaidya): apply knowledge, pharmacology, procedural skill, and clinical judgment',
      'Sadhyasadhya assessment: Sadhya (curable) - treat with confidence. Yapya (manageable) - treat for symptom control. Asadhya (incurable) - do not treat or treat symptomatically',
      'Timing (Kriyakala): early treatment in Chaya-Prakopa stages for best results; later stages are progressively more difficult',
      'Treatment must be individualized - same disease in different patients needs different approaches based on Prakriti, Bala, Agni',
