    additionalTopics: [
      { title: 'Panchakarma Pradhana Karma', content: 'Five main procedures: (1) Vamana - for Kapha, morning. (2) Virechana - for Pitta, afternoon. (3) Basti - for Vata, morning/evening. (4) Nasya - for head region, morning. (5) Raktamokshana - for Rakta-Pitta. Each targets specific Dosha and location.', clinicalRelevance: 'Correct Panchakarma selection based on disease is essential.' },
      { title: 'Samsarjana Krama (Post-Panchakarma Diet)', content: 'Graduated diet after Shodhana: Day 1-2: Peya (thin gruel). Day 3-4: Vilepi (thick gruel). Day 5-6: Akrita Yusha + Mamsa Rasa. Day 7: Krita Yusha + normal diet. Purpose: gradually restore Agni weakened by Shodhana.', clinicalRelevance: 'Samsarjana Krama is essential for Agni restoration after Panchakarma.' },
    ],
    importantVerses: [
      'Snehana and Swedana are the preparatory procedures before Shodhana (15.3)',
      'Internal oleation: Ghrita for Pitta, Taila for Vata, Vasa for Vata-Kapha, Majja for severe Vata (15.4)',
      'Signs of proper Snehana: soft stools, clarity of senses, lightness, Agni improvement (15.8)',
      'Signs of proper Swedana: sweating, pain relief, lightness, stiffness reduction (15.9)',
      'Samsarjana Krama: Peya to regular diet over 7 days (15.10)',
      'Panchakarma has three stages: Poorvakarma, Pradhana Karma, Paschat Karma (15.12)',
    ],
